# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# LINE ENDINGS ARE A DEPLOYMENT CONCERN HERE, not a style preference.
#
# index.html carries an inline JSON-LD block whose CSP hash is pinned in
# vercel.json. A CSP hash covers the exact bytes the browser receives.
# Git stores this repo with LF and Vercel builds on Linux, so the
# deployed bytes are LF — but a Windows checkout is CRLF by default, and
# a hash computed from that working copy matches locally and matches
# nothing in production. That is not hypothetical: it shipped, and the
# browser silently dropped the structured data on the live site while
# every local check passed.
#
# Pinning the whole tree to LF means the working copy, the repo, and the
# deployed file are byte-identical, so a hash computed anywhere is the
# hash the browser will check.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
